# Modular new code

Design all **new** types with one job and clean boundaries. Do not grow `MainForm`, `RibbonMenu`, or other large files into monoliths.

## Separation

- Put business logic, commands, and services in their own files.
- Keep UI wiring thin: the form or control calls a service; it does not own the algorithm.
- Follow MVVM-style separation (model / logic / view) even in WinForms. Do not convert the existing app to WPF unless asked.

## How to add a feature

- New file or small class per concern (e.g. `CadShortcuts.cs`, `CadToolTip.cs`, `CaptionFrame.cs`).
- Prefer a dedicated service or helper over another 100 lines in an existing code-behind.
- Reuse existing helpers (`AppIcons`, `CadToolTip`, `CaptionFrame`) instead of copying their logic.

## Single responsibility

- One class, one reason to change.
- New code must integrate without rewriting or polluting working chrome, shortcuts, or tooltips.
- If a change needs shared state, add a small service; do not dump fields onto `MainForm`.
